  "term": "continuous spectrum",
  "definition": "A continuous spectrum is a way of understanding a condition or trait as varying gradually across a range rather than falling into sharply separated categories. In the source, it refers to metabolic dysfunction progressing through degrees of change instead of only being identified by fixed cutoff points.",
